  "$instructions": {
    "general": [
      "Extract ordinance requirements ONLY for large, commercial, or utility-scale solar energy systems (typically intended for offsite electricity generation or sale, often 1MW+ or above specified thresholds). Do NOT extract requirements that apply only to small, micro, private, personal, onsite, or residential systems, or to meteorological towers.",
      "Use direct text excerpts and quotes in the summary field as much as possible. If multiple options exist and you make a selection, list all other options and their conditions in the summary.",
      "Only extract explicit requirements that have been enacted. Do not extract definitions unless they also constitute requirements.",
      "Pay careful attention to clarifying text in parentheses, footnotes, and cross-references.",
      "When multiple values are mentioned for the same feature, select the most restrictive value (largest minimum, lowest maximum, etc.) and note the other options in the summary.",
      "Ensure units are expressed using standard, conventional names (e.g., 'feet', 'meters', 'dBA', 'hr/year', 'tip-height-multiplier').",
      "Every row must include an ordinance_text holding the complete relevant excerpt for the ordinance being extracted, copy-pasted verbatim from the source document. Its first sentence must be the start of the ordinance text for this extraction, reproduced in full; after that first sentence an ellipsis ('...') may be used to drop irrelevant passages. ordinance_text is never paraphrased or normalized — every character outside the ellipses appears exactly as written in the source.",
      "Every row must include an explanation that briefly justifies why the cited summary evidence matches the selected feature under this schema's rules.",
      "Emit only positively matched features. Never emit a row to explain why a feature does not apply.",
      "For features where no requirement exists, set value, units, and summary to null (omit the feature from the array entirely, or include it with null values).",
      "The outputs array is a sparse long-form extraction table and does not need to contain every enumerated feature.",
      "Tables, table footnotes, and labeled graphics count as valid ordinance evidence when they state the controlling requirement; preserve the relevant table cell or footnote context in summary.",
      "If ordinance text shows an amended or superseding requirement, extract the current operative requirement as written rather than a superseded historical value unless the ordinance text clearly keeps both rules active.",
      "If text is suggestive but not explicit for the target feature, omit the feature."
    ],
    "setback_specific": [
      "For distance-based setbacks, extract the numerical value and units (feet/meters).",
      "If text includes an adder (e.g., 'multiplier × height + X feet'), note this in the summary. Adder values should be converted to feet.",
      "If text includes conditional minimums ('the greater of', 'no less than'), note minimum threshold in summary.",
      "If text includes conditional maximums ('the lesser of', 'no more than'), note maximum limit in summary.",
      "For structures and property lines: Check if ordinance distinguishes between participating and non-participating owners. If yes, extract separate values for each. If no distinction, use the non-participating feature for the general setback.",
      "For roads: Verify the requirement is truly for roads and not better classified as a property line setback.",
      "When one setback clause explicitly names multiple target features and provides one shared numeric threshold, emit one row per explicitly named feature using the same threshold and units."
    ],
    "restriction_specific": [
      "For numerical solar restrictions: Extract the numerical value and units specified by the feature definition. If multiple comparable values exist, select the most restrictive and retain other values and their conditions in summary.",
      "For maximum height: Extract the maximum solar panel or structure height, preserving the measurement origin and any panel-angle condition. Exclude minimum ground clearance, fencing heights, rooftop-only limits, and system-class definition thresholds.",
      "For maximum project size: Specify in summary whether the limit is capacity-based (MW, kW, etc.) or count-based (systems or panels). Exclude area-only limits and thresholds that merely trigger approval for larger projects; retain independent capacity and count limits without comparing their raw numbers.",
      "For minimum/maximum lot size: Extract solar lot, parcel, or tract area limits, not linear dimensions, coverage percentages, or capacity limits.",
      "For panel spacing: Only extract explicit minimum spacing between individual solar panels. Do not infer spacing from setbacks, land density, or coverage, and do not classify it as separation between solar farms.",
      "For land density: Only extract explicit maximum solar capacity per unit land area, preserving the stated capacity/area units. Exclude inverse density (area per capacity), absolute capacity or area limits, and density inferred from setbacks.",
      "For coverage: Extract the maximum land coverage percentage or fraction as stated. Do not infer coverage from lot area, capacity, or land density.",
      "For qualitative solar restrictions: Retain the full relevant provisions in ordinance_text and use direct excerpts and quotes in summary, with value and units null. Explicit nonregulation follows the feature rules for ENR.",
      "For prohibitions: Only extract enacted, currently effective, unconditional jurisdiction-wide solar bans or moratoria. If solar is allowed through an approval route, this is not a prohibition. Classify district-only bans under prohibited use districts."
    ],
    "district_specific": [
      "For permitted use districts: Extract array of district names/codes. Consider overlay districts as primary use.",
      "For special use districts: Include districts requiring board approval, special permits, or conditional use permits.",
      "For accessory use districts: Include districts where solar is only allowed as accessory/secondary to another use.",
      "For prohibited use districts: Only include districts with unconditional prohibitions currently in effect.",
      "Use the exact district names/codes as they appear in the ordinance text."
    ]
  },
  "$qa_checklist": [
    "Examples are sparse response fragments. Do not pad them with null rows. Review every enum feature for coverage and emit each explicitly supported feature at most once.",
    "Feature IDs are unique and no row explains mere absence. For documents with no extractable in-scope features outputs is empty.",
    "Every row has non-null, nonempty summary, ordinance_text, and explanation supporting the same explicit enacted provision for the selected solar class and feature.",
    "Numeric values have matching units. Formula strings preserve every adder, bound, and condition with units embedded and units=null. ENR has an explicit supporting nonregulation quote and units=null.",
    "No waiver is converted to zero, no permit threshold is mistaken for a capacity cap, and no panel spacing is classified as inter-farm separation.",
    "Coverage is percent/fraction, lot size is area, and land density is capacity per area. Do not infer one from another.",
    "Qualitative obligations have null value/units and source evidence. The only null-valued numerical-feature rows describe explicit participating waivers; other numerical rows require a threshold, a complete formula, or explicitly supported ENR. Omit unsupported features.",
    "District lists reflect exact names, table legends, and conditions."
  ],
  "$qualitative_features": [
    "prohibitions",
    "decommissioning",
    "glare",
    "visual impact",
    "repowering",
    "fencing",
    "signage",
    "screening",
